  "597060": [
   {
    "old": "<img alt=\"Four-step figure for drawing butane. Step 1: draw the carbon chain C-C-C-C. Step 2: give each carbon four bonds by adding H atoms (the Lewis or expanded formula). Step 3: condense the H atoms onto each carbon with subscripts, CH3CH2CH2CH3 (the condensed formula). Step 4: draw a zigzag line with carbons at the ends and corners (the skeletal formula); H atoms on each carbon equal 4 minus the number of bonds shown. Red arrows connect the steps.\" class=\"internal\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/437067/clipboard_ead8b802fccf8dc28ff59696821f2f298.png\" fileid=\"437067\" />",
    "new": "<img alt=\"Four-step figure for drawing butane. Step 1: draw the carbon chain C-C-C-C. Step 2: give each carbon four bonds by adding H atoms (the Lewis or expanded formula). Step 3: condense the H atoms onto each carbon with subscripts, CH3CH2CH2CH3 (the condensed formula). Step 4: draw a zigzag line with carbons at the ends and corners (the skeletal formula); H atoms on each carbon equal 4 minus the number of bonds shown. Red arrows connect the steps.\" class=\"internal\" src=\"/@api/deki/files/{{s1}}/fig-p597060-steps-butane.png\" fileid=\"{{s1}}\" />",
    "count": 1,
    "note": "1.7 Example 1 steps: also, This is the"
   },
